*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* Target: Extended BASIC disk
*
* Builds     dist/disk-xb/{{STEM}}.dsk holding LOAD and {{XBNAME}}
* Requires   Extended BASIC cartridge + 32K expansion + disk
*            (no Editor/Assembler)
*
*   RUN "DSK1.LOAD"
*
* Extended BASIC was in far more homes than the Editor/Assembler module,
* so this is usually the disk that reaches the most people.
*
* XB is only the loader here. ../../boot/LOAD.b99 does CALL LOAD to read
* this object, then CALL LINK("XBBOOT") to enter it, and we never return.
*
* Taking the machine matters because XB does not simply step aside. It
* keeps interpreter state across scratchpad and installs its own
* interrupt routine, and a program written for a cartridge expects both
* to be its own. Interrupts go off first, then the two locations that
* let XB back in are cleared. Appendix 24.3.1 of the Editor/Assembler
* manual documents them: a flag byte controlling the interrupt routine,
* and the address of the user-defined interrupt routine.
*
* What survives is the console's own interrupt routine, doing only its
* built-in work - the timer, sprite motion, and the sound list. That is
* what a cartridge program already relies on, which is why the shared
* body needs no changes for this target.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
       DEF  MAIN,XBBOOT

XBBOOT LIMI 0                * Before anything else: stop XB's interrupt
*                              routine running while we take the machine
*                              apart underneath it.

       LWPI WRKSP            * Our own workspace, not XB's

       CLR  R0
       MOV  R0,@>83C4        * Address of the user interrupt routine
       MOVB R0,@>83C2        * Flag byte controlling the interrupt routine
       MOVB R0,@>837A        * No sprites in automatic motion

* The keyboard scan copies >83D4 into VDP register 1 whenever it sees a
* new key, so keep that byte matching what REGLD sets.
       LI   R0,>E000
       MOVB R0,@>83D4

       B    @MAIN

       COPY "../main.a99"
